    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d691">

                <pb facs="1122" n="1106" sameAs="frus:frus1951v07p1/pg1106"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">
                    S/S Files: NSC
                    118</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Executive Secretary of the National
                        Security Council</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Lay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the National Security Council
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        NSC 118</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1951-11-09">November 9, 1951</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Courses of Action in Korea</hi>
                </p>
                <p>
                    <table>
                        <row role="label">
                            <cell rendition="#top">References:</cell>
                            <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">A. NSC
                                Action No. 562<anchor n="1" xml:id="d691-f1"/>
                            </cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell/>
                            <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">B. Memo for NSC from Acting Executive Secretary, same subject,
                                dated September 5, 1951<anchor n="2" xml:id="d691-f2"/>
                            </cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell/>
                            <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">C. Progress Report, dated September
                                25, 1951 by the Secretaries of State and Defense on NSC 48/5<anchor n="3" xml:id="d691-f3"
                                />
                            </cell>
                        </row>
                    </table>
                </p>
                <p>At the request of the Acting Secretary of Defense, the enclosed memorandum by the
                    Joint Chiefs of Staff on the subject is circulated herewith for the information
                    of the National Security Council with <pb facs="1123" n="1107" xml:id="pg1107"/>
                    reference to NSC Action No. 562–<hi
                        rendition="#italic">a</hi>, and is referred to the Senior NSC Staff for consideration in connection with
                        NSC Action No. 562–<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >b</hi>.</p>
                <p>In transmitting the enclosure, the Acting Secretary of Defense stated that he
                    concurred with it and invited particular attention to paragraph 9 therein.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">James</hi> S. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lay</hi>, <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jr</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d691-a1.xml" xpointer="d691-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
